================================================================================
TEST 38396 — Route table is synced across the stack
================================================================================
Date        : 2026-08-19
Bench       : tb470
DUT         : AT-IE520-28GSX two-member VCStack, virtual-chassis-id 3439,
              VMAC 0000.cd37.0d6f
              member 1 = S/N 264A23066, MAC 84e3.2787.0740, console /dev/u5
              member 2 = S/N 264A23052, MAC 84e3.2787.09c0, console /dev/u4
Software    : IE520-tb470.rel (IE520-tomahawk_ie520-continuous.rel, 2026-08-19)
Companion   : run immediately after test 38393 (FDB sync) on the same rig; see
              38393.log for the LAG build and the bootloader netboot finding.

VERDICT: ALL 7 STEPS PASS.
         The route table is synced across both stack members, before and after a
         master reboot, in BOTH the software route table (show ip route) and the
         hardware route table (show platform table ip). Worst-case traffic
         outage across the master reboot was 883 ms against a 6-second
         expectation.
         One benign post-reboot difference in a software allocation index is
         documented under STEP 7 — it is not a sync failure.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
